      "writtenOn": "2026-11-19T13:51:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The verdict only exists if the run reaches the outermost `test-end`. If it ends without getting there, the program finishes with status 0 and the test passes, with every failure it recorded unreported. That happens if an upstream update adds a `test-begin` without its `test-end`, or a `skipped-lines.txt` entry blanks one.\n\nA cheap guard: have `conformance.rs` require the summary line in the output, or have the shim exit non-zero unless it was printed (for instance `(exit 2)` as the file\u0027s last form, which a correct run never reaches because `test-end` exits first). Requiring a minimum number of passed cases would also catch a suite that silently shrank.",
      "revId": "205a979ad8a12e11bf56297206a24b00b168602e",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
